{"id": "EUVD-2026-28749", "enisaUuid": "9b219a43-19a2-3929-a40a-dd042d8656b3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: amd: acp-mach-common: Add missing error check for clock acquisition\n\nThe acp_card_rt5682_init() and acp_card_rt5682s_init() functions did not\ncheck the return values of clk_get(). This could lead to a kernel crash\nwhen the invalid pointers are later dereferenced by clock core\nfunctions.\n\nFix this by:\n1. Changing clk_get() to the device-managed devm_clk_get().\n2. Adding IS_ERR() checks immediately after each clock acquisition.", "datePublished": "2026-05-08T14:22:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a71ce398347fed9422dbd5c6458f7f8348012c64", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/53682a55cac6f159311c63d04f3d7ba64a8a455a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0e31a7ed1191c12a28763bb70c4c7f5adadc79d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0cee68fb7f4cf1562e067c5a82d25062a973b0d0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/30c64fb9839949f085c8eb55b979cbd8a4c51f00"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-43443", "GHSA-xx4x-7c38-rpq3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "10cb78d2-6322-3bd8-bc6f-de01057de6df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4c750f2c7d44b5b39e197308bc3f510205bba4b <0cee68fb7f4cf1562e067c5a82d25062a973b0d0"}, {"id": "3cf75d4a-2bcd-37e9-94a0-07a869d50008", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4c750f2c7d44b5b39e197308bc3f510205bba4b <e0e31a7ed1191c12a28763bb70c4c7f5adadc79d"}, {"id": "5e72aa6e-0301-37de-93ce-56a886d4dddd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "849a129a-7ff2-3fad-92a5-35a15fb48218", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4c750f2c7d44b5b39e197308bc3f510205bba4b <30c64fb9839949f085c8eb55b979cbd8a4c51f00"}, {"id": 